course: dictionary
lesson: 5975
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Maya with a capital letter can name a people, a language, or a girl. Look at the clues around it: is the sentence about history, a friend, or a language?
explain: «The ancient Maya built step pyramids and stone cities.» The clues are ancient, pyramids and cities, so Maya means a people of Central America. Mayan, the adjective, describes things that belong to them, like Mayan languages.
explain: «Maya smiled, but her eyes stayed sad.» Here Maya is a girl's name. Check it by swapping in «she»: the sentence still makes sense, so Maya is a person in the story. A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Maya is a noun for a people of Central America, such as southern Mexico, Guatemala and Belize.
fact: The ancient Maya built stone cities and step pyramids, such as Chichen Itza and Tikal.
fact: The Maya had a full writing system of glyphs, carved on stone and painted in folding books made of bark.
fact: Maya is also a girl's name, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Maya people still live in Central America today, and many speak Mayan languages.
exercise: «The ancient Maya built a great step pyramid in the forest.» In this sentence, what does Maya name? | *A people of Central America | A king's palace | A girl's name | A river in the forest
exercise: «Maya smiled, but her eyes stayed sad.» Which meaning of Maya fits here? | A type of bird | *A girl's name | A stone city | A language of Central America
exercise: «Many people still speak Mayan languages today.» What word is Mayan in this sentence? | A girl's name | *An adjective that describes the languages | A kind of pyramid | A city in Mexico
test: Which sentence uses Maya as a girl's name? | Maya cities in the north kept going for many years | The Maya had a full writing system of glyphs | *Maya's friend said she would run away that night | The Maya grew maize and cacao
test: «Later Maya cities in the north, like Chichen Itza, kept going.» What is Chichen Itza? | A girl's name | A river in Denver | A kind of pasta | *A Maya city with a great pyramid
exam: «The ancient Maya civilisation had calendars and writing.» Which meaning of Maya fits this sentence? | A type of food | *A people of Central America with an ancient civilisation | A girl's name | A river in Mexico
